Read the function table with atomic loads

init_functable fills the table with atomic stores, on whichever thread
first calls through one of its stubs, while other threads may already
be calling through it: two threads inflating PNGs at once is enough.
Every call reads its entry with a plain load, which beside an atomic
store is a data race, and ThreadSanitizer reports one for each entry
the first calls touch.

Read each entry with a relaxed atomic load. Every value an entry holds
is a function that can be called, its stub or the one chosen, so there
is nothing for an ordering to order; on x86-64 and ARM64 a relaxed load
is the same instruction as a plain one. Compilers without the GNU
atomic builtins keep the plain load, as they keep their own store.

